{
  "about": [
    "What real CEF 152.0.5 told the window's load handler for one main-frame navigation per case, what the window then tells the tab, and what `tabs` and `diagnose` read (t-125617).",
    "Measured 2026-11-22 off screen, with the installed window's own engine files and a loopback server, by a probe hosted like fixtures/chromium-popup/probe. Navigations were DevTools Page.navigate, as the window sends them.",
    "`engine` lists the load handler's calls in the order CEF made them: `start` (on_load_start), `end` (on_load_end, with its HTTP status) and `error` (on_load_error, with its code). A call is for the main frame and for the address the tab was sent to unless it says otherwise.",
    "`from` is the record the case began on: `open` (a pane just opened at the address), `page` (a page that loaded) or the case just before it.",
    "A case is a navigation the window sent to its address, which the window records before sending, unless `by` names a step that sends no address: `back` and `forward` (the window's buttons, browser.go_back · go_forward) or `reload` (browser.reload). `EARLIER` is the page the history step returns to, `NEWER` a later navigation inside the case. The load handler drops a main-frame error for an address other than the one the pane records (on_load_error's address check) (t-125843).",
    "The back, forward, same-address and reload cases (t-125843) were measured the same way with the pane born as the window bears it: on about:blank, in a request context of its own, with the window's disabled features; twice in each of two runs, all four alike.",
    "`before` is what 1.1.172 told the tab (browser:nav) for the same calls, and what the window still tells it, word for word (t-125903). `tabs` is the word `zerocode-browser tabs` says after, `failure` the error `diagnose` names: only the pane's record keeps a refusal.",
    "Read by crates/zerocode-shell/src/main_unit_tests.rs (cef_failed_navigation_tests), which replays `engine` through chromium_browser::heard."
  ],
